# The uncaught twin of unit_null_struct_deref_catch: a field read through an own reference holding nothing, no handler --
# the implicit `interpreter` throw leaves the method and the unit; R0 is stopped (Fails 1, Stopped 1, Thrown 4).  Natively
# and with the methods walked.
Model: (int: v 11; int: spare 99)
fn: r () int
    @: Model box
    return: box\v
end: r
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
